{"root":"pli/ms","translators":["sujato"],"title":"The Little Financier: a past life story","html":"<article id='ja4'><header><ul><li class='division'><span class='root'>Jātaka </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Stories of Past Lives 4 </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Ekakanipāta </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The Book of the Ones </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Apaṇṇakavagga </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Sure Bet </span></li></ul>\n<h1 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>4. Cūḷaseṭṭhijātaka </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The Little Financier: a past life story </span></h1></header>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>“Appakenapi medhāvī, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Even with a little capital </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>pābhatena vicakkhaṇo; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>the intelligent and clear-seeing man </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Samuṭṭhāpeti attānaṁ, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>uplifts himself, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>aṇuṁ aggiṁva sandhaman”ti. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>like a tiny flame when fanned. </span></span></p></blockquote>\n<p class='endsutta'><span class='root'>Cūḷaseṭṭhijātakaṁ catutthaṁ. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></p></article>"}
